{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"59c1c263","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005782,"end_time":"2026-08-16T17:26:40.359514+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-16T17:26:40.353732+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Real-Time Lightweight Deepfake Audio Detection using Tiny SSL + Lightweight CNN\n","\n","**BTP (B.Tech Project) — Research Notebook**\n","\n","### Objective\n","This notebook implements and trains a **binary audio deepfake detector** (Real vs. Fake / Bonafide vs. Spoof)\n","on the **ASVspoof2024** dataset, designed to be **lightweight enough for real-time / edge deployment**.\n","\n","### Architecture\n","\n","```\n","Input Audio\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Voice Activity Detection (VAD)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Log-Mel Spectrogram (80-dim)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Tiny SSL Encoder (DistilHuBERT)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Lightweight CNN (MobileNetV3-Small / EfficientNet-Lite0)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Wavelet Block (optional, PyWavelets DWT fusion)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Self-Attention Pooling\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Classifier Head (Linear → Dropout → GELU → Linear)\n","    │\n","    ▼\n","Real / Fake\n","```\n","\n","### Key Design Goals\n","1. **Low latency / low parameter count** — suitable for real-time inference on commodity or edge hardware.\n","2. **Self-supervised speech representations** distilled into a tiny encoder (DistilHuBERT) to retain\n","   robust phonetic/prosodic cues used by SOTA anti-spoofing systems, without the cost of full HuBERT/Wav2Vec2.\n","3. **CNN backbone reuse** (MobileNetV3-Small / EfficientNet-Lite0) treats the SSL feature sequence as a\n","   2D \"image\" to exploit efficient, well-optimized vision architectures for local artifact detection.\n","4. **Optional wavelet-domain fusion** to capture multi-resolution spectral artifacts characteristic of\n","   vocoder-based synthesis (a known deepfake signature).\n","5. **Attention pooling** for a variable-length-robust, discriminative utterance-level embedding.\n","\n","### Dataset\n","**ASVspoof 2024 (LA/DF track)** — bonafide vs. spoofed speech utterances with official train/dev/eval\n","protocol files.\n","\n","### Reproducibility\n","All experiments use a fixed random seed, deterministic data splits (as defined by ASVspoof protocol files),\n","and full configuration logging (see `CONFIG` in Cell 5).\n","\n","---\n","*Framework: PyTorch, torchaudio, HuggingFace Transformers, torchvision, timm, PyWavelets, librosa, scikit-learn.*"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"6d6959e3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-16T17:26:40.37027Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-16T17:26:40.369464Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-16T17:26:40.373837Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-16T17:26:40.373225Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.011222,"end_time":"2026-08-16T17:26:40.375339+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-16T17:26:40.364117+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ==============================================================\n","# Cell 2: Install dependencies\n","# ==============================================================\n","# Run this once. In Colab/Kaggle/local Jupyter with internet access.\n","# Comment out lines for packages you already have installed.\n","\n","# %pip install -q torch torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121\n","# %pip install -q torchvision\n","# %pip install -q transformers>=4.40.0\n","# %pip install -q timm\n","# %pip install -q librosa\n","# %pip install -q PyWavelets\n","# %pip install -q scikit-learn\n","# %pip install -q pandas numpy matplotlib tqdm\n","# %pip install -q soundfile\n","# %pip install -q onnx onnxruntime\n","# # Optional (only needed if you want WebRTC-based VAD instead of the built-in energy-based VAD):\n","# %pip install -q webrtcvad"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"6c8edbae","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-16T17:26:40.38565Z","iopub.status.busy"